he Union''s duty to protect states; Article 353 deals with the effect of proclamation of Emergency. See table below for the complete Article-wise list.","table":{"headers":["Article Number","Subject Matter"],"rows":[["352","Proclamation of Emergency"],["353","Effect of Proclamation of Emergency"],["354","Distribution of revenues during Emergency"],["355","Duty of the Union to protect states against external aggression and internal disturbance"],["356","Provisions in case of failure of constitutional machinery in states"],["357","Exercise of legislative powers under proclamation issued under Article 356"],["358","Suspension of provisions of Article 19 during Emergencies"],["359","Suspension of enforcement of Part III rights during Emergencies"],["359A","Application to Punjab (Repealed)"],["360","Provisions as to Financial Emergency"]]},"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Article 356 – Provisions in case of failure of constitutional machinery in states","b":"Article 357 – Provisions as to Financial Emergency","c":"Article 353 – Duty of the Union to protect states","d":"Article 355 – Suspension of provisions of Article 19 during Emergencies"},"answer":"a"}]') ON CONFLICT(chapter_slug) DO UPDATE SET subject_id=excluded.subject_id, chapter_number=excluded.chapter_number, title=excluded.title, answers_json=excluded.answers_json;
