hree","d":"Four"},"answer":"d"},{"a":"The President''s","e":"The Governor has no further role once such a bill is presented again; only the President''s assent is needed.","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"The Governor''s","b":"The President''s","c":"Both the Governor''s and President''s","d":"The Chief Minister''s"},"answer":"b"},{"a":"Three","e":"The Governor may assent, withhold assent, or reserve the money bill for the President''s consideration; unlike ordinary bills, there is no option to return it for reconsideration.","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Three","b":"Four","c":"Five","d":"Two"},"answer":"a"},{"a":"Suspensive veto","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Pocket veto","b":"Qualified veto","c":"Suspensive veto","d":"Absolute veto"},"answer":"c"},{"a":"I and II only","e":"Unlike the President, the Governor cannot make an ordinance without instructions from the President in three specified cases.","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"I, II and III","b":"I only","c":"II and III only","d":"I and II only"},"answer":"d"},{"a":"Six weeks","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Six weeks","b":"Eight weeks","c":"Twelve weeks","d":"Four weeks"},"answer":"a"},{"a":"The legislative council","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"The Chief Minister","b":"The President","c":"The Governor","d":"The legislative council"},"answer":"d"},{"a":"Death sentence","e":"The power to grant pardon for a death sentence lies with the President alone; however, the Governor can suspend, remit, or commute a death sentence.","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Fine","b":"Community service","c":"Imprisonment","d":"Death sentence"},"answer":"d"},{"a":"Pardon, reprieve or remission in respect of court-martial sentences","e":"The Governor does not possess any power relating to sentences awarded by a court-martial (military court); this power rests solely with the President.","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Pardon for of