his tenure up to five years in total, through annual extensions of up to one year each, not exceeding three such extensions.","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Two years","b":"Three years","c":"Five years","d":"Four years"},"answer":"a"},{"a":"Five years","e":"Extensions can be granted up to one year at a time, in public interest, on the recommendation of the appointing Committee, with reasons recorded in writing.","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Six years","b":"Five years","c":"Four years","d":"Three years"},"answer":"b"},{"a":"Joint Secretary","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Deputy Secretary","b":"Under Secretary","c":"Additional Secretary","d":"Joint Secretary"},"answer":"d"},{"a":"Article 14","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Article 19","b":"Article 32","c":"Article 14","d":"Article 21"},"answer":"c"},{"a":"Delhi Special Police Establishment Act, 1946","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"NIA Act, 2008","b":"CVC Act, 2003","c":"Prevention of Corruption Act, 1988","d":"Delhi Special Police Establishment Act, 1946"},"answer":"d"},{"a":"National Central Bureau of Interpol","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"National Central Bureau of Interpol","b":"Nodal agency for NIA","c":"National Crime Records Bureau","d":"National Vigilance Bureau"},"answer":"a"},{"a":"Sweden","e":"The institution of Ombudsman was first created in Sweden in 1809; ''Ombud'' is a Swedish term referring to a person who acts as a representative or spokesman of another.","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Sweden","b":"United Kingdom","c":"Finland","d":"New Zealand"},"answer":"a"},{"a":"New Zealand","e":"New Zealand adopted this in 1962; the United Kingdom adopted a similar institution called the Parliamentary Commissioner for Administration in 1967.","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"New Zealand","b":"Australia","c":"Canada","d":"United Kingdom"},"answer":"a"},{"a":"I and II only","e":"Unlike New Zealand''s Lokpal-Lokayukta model, in Sweden the judiciary is within the purview of the Ombudsman.","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"I and III only","b":"I, II and III","c":"II and III only","d":"I and II only"},"answer":"d"},{"a":"Procurator System","e":"The French system of Administrative Courts is another distinct institutional device, which spread to other countries due to its success in France.","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Ombudsman System","b":"Commissioner System","c":"Procurator System","d":"Administrative Courts System"},"answer":"c"},{"a":"First Administrative Reforms Commission","e":"The First ARC (1966–1970) recommended these institutions on the pattern of the Ombudsman in Scandinavian countries and the parliamentary commissioner for investigation in New Zealand.","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Balwantrai Mehta Committee","b":"First Administrative Reforms Commission","c":"Second Administrative Reforms Commission","d":"Law Commission of India"},"answer":"b"},{"a":"Ministers and Secretaries at Central and state levels","e":"The lokayukta (one at the Centre and one in every state) would deal with complaints against other specified higher officials; the ARC kept the judiciary outside the purview of Lokpal and lokayukta.","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Only Members of Parliament","b":"State Chief Ministers only","c":"Ministers and Secretaries at Central and state levels","d":"Only judiciary officials"},"answer":"c"},{"a":"President, after consultation with the Chief Justice of India, the Speaker of Lok Sabha and the Chairman of the Rajya Sabha","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Chief Justice of India alone","b":"Parliament through a resolution","c":"Prime Minister alone","d":"President, after consultation with the Chief Justice of India, the Speaker of Lok Sabha and the Chairman of the Rajya Sabha"},"answer":"d"},{"a":"2013","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"2011","b":"2012","c":"2013","d":"2014"},"answer":"c"},{"a":"Congress Government headed by Indira Gandhi","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"NDA Government headed by A.B. Vajpayee","b":"Janata Government headed by Morarji Desai","c":"Congress Government headed by Indira Gandhi","d":"National Front Government headed by V.P. Singh"},"answer":"c"},{"a":"I, II and III","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"I and II only","b":"I and III only","c":"II and III only","d":"I, II and III"},"answer":"d"},{"a":"An eminent jurist nominated by the President","e":"This eminent jurist is nominated by the President on the basis of recommendations of the first four members of the Selection Committee. A Search Committee, with 50% membership from SCs/STs/OBCs/minorities/women, assists the Selection Committee.","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"The Chief Election Commissioner","b":"An eminent jurist nominated by the President","c":"The Comptroller and Auditor General","d":"The Attorney General of India"},"answer":"b"},{"a":"Prime Minister","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Prime Minister","b":"Speaker of the Lok Sabha","c":"Central Vigilance Commissioner","d":"Chief Justice of India"},"answer":"a"},{"a":"Ten years","e":"The Act enhanced the maximum punishment from seven years to ten years, and raised the minimum punishment under sections 7, 8, 9 and 12 to three years.","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Ten years","b":"Seven years","c":"Twelve years","d":"Five years"},"answer":"a"},{"a":"₹10 lakhs","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"₹5 lakhs","b":"₹1 crore","c":"₹10 lakhs","d":"₹20 lakhs"},"answer":"c"},{"a":"365 days","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"180 days","b":"90 days","c":"365 days","d":"730 days"},"answer":"c"},{"a":"Lokpal cannot proceed suo motu against any public servant","e":"Other drawbacks include disallowing anonymous complaints, a 7-year limitation period for filing complaints, and a non-transparent procedure for complaints against the PM.","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Lokpal has no power over the CBI","b":"Lokpal cannot investigate Group A officers","c":"Lokpal cannot receive complaints against Ministers","d":"Lokpal cannot proceed suo motu against any public servant"},"answer":"d"},{"a":"7 years","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"5 years","b":"7 years","c":"3 years","d":"10 years"},"answer":"b"},{"a":"Maharashtra","e":"Maharashtra established its lokayukta in 1971, though Odisha had passed the enabling Act in 1970.","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Maharashtra","b":"Uttar Pradesh","c":"Odisha","d":"Bihar"},"answer":"a"},{"a":"I and III only","e":"While the term of office in most states is 5 years or 65 years of age (whichever is earlier), this is not uniform across all states, so statement (II) is incorrect.","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"I and II only","b":"I and III only","c":"I, II and III","d":"II and III only"},"answer":"b"},{"a":"Governor of the state","e":"The Governor places this report, along with an explanatory memorandum, before the state legislature.","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Chief Justice of the High Court","b":"Chief Minister of the state","c":"State Legislative Assembly Speaker","d":"Governor of the state"},"answer":"d"},{"a":"2009","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"2011","b":"2008","c":"2009","d":"2010"},"answer":"c"},{"a":"2008 Mumbai terror attacks (26/11)","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"1993 Mumbai bomb blasts","b":"2001 Parliament attack","c":"2008 Mumbai terror attacks (26/11)","d":"2016 Uri attack"},"answer":"c"},{"a":"New Delhi","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Kolkata","b":"Mumbai","c":"Hyderabad","d":"New Delhi"},"answer":"d"},{"a":"TFFC Cell","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Anti-Terror Cell","b":"TFFC Cell","c":"Terror Finance Wing","d":"FICN Cell"},"answer":"b"},{"a":"Director-General","e":"The Director-General''s powers are similar to those exercisable by a Director-General of Police in respect of the police force in a state; he/she is appointed by the Central Government.","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Director","b":"Director-General","c":"Commissioner","d":"Inspector-General"},"answer":"b"},{"a":"Ministry of Home Affairs","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Ministry of Defence","b":"Ministry of Home Affairs","c":"Ministry of Law and Justice","d":"Ministry of Personnel"},"answer":"b"},{"a":"Second Administrative Reforms Commission","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"National Police Commission","b":"First Administrative Reforms Commission","c":"Law Commission of India","d":"Second Administrative Reforms Commission"},"answer":"d"},{"a":"2019","e":"This extension was made through the NIA (Amendment) Act, 2019.","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"2008","b":"2009","c":"2019","d":"2021"},"answer":"c"},{"a":"I, II and III","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"I, II and III","b":"I and II only","c":"II and III only","d":"I and III only"},"answer":"a"},{"a":"Terror attacks under its concurrent jurisdiction","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Economic offences","b":"Cyber-terrorism only","c":"Human trafficking cases","d":"Terror attacks under its concurrent jurisdiction"},"answer":"d"},{"a":"Indian Ocean tsunami of 2004","e":"A High Powered Committee had been set up in 1999 and a National Committee in 2001 (after the Gujarat earthquake) even before the Act was enacted.","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Bhopal gas tragedy","b":"Gujarat earthquake","c":"Odisha super cyclone","d":"Indian Ocean tsunami of 2004"},"answer":"d"},{"a":"2006","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"2005","b":"2008","c":"2007","d":"2006"},"answer":"d"},{"a":"Prime Minister","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Prime Minister","b":"President of India","c":"Cabinet Secretary","d":"Union Home Minister"},"answer":"a"},{"a":"Nine","e":"The other members are nominated by the chairperson; one of them is designated as vice-chairperson, who holds the status of a Cabinet Minister, while the remaining members hold the status of a Minister of State.","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Nine","b":"Ten","c":"Seven","d":"Eight"},"answer":"a"},{"a":"Union Ministry of Home Affairs","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Union Ministry of Personnel","b":"Union Ministry of Home Affairs","c":"Union Ministry of Rural Development","d":"Union Ministry of Environment"},"answer":"b"},{"a":"National Disaster Response Force (NDRF)","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"National Disaster Response Force (NDRF)","b":"Border Security Force","c":"National Security Guard","d":"Central Industrial Security Force"},"answer":"a"},{"a":"NDMA","e":"The National Institute of Disaster Management is located in New Delhi.","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"NDMA","b":"SDMA","c":"DDMA","d":"Union Ministry of Home Affairs"},"answer":"a"},{"a":"Chief Minister of the state","e":"The chairperson of the State Executive Committee is an ex-officio member of the SDMA and also acts as its ex-officio chief executive officer.","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Governor of the state","b":"Chief Secretary of the state","c":"Home Minister of the state","d":"Chief Minister of the state"},"answer":"d"},{"a":"Eight","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Seven","b":"Six","c":"Nine","d":"Eight"},"answer":"d"},{"a":"Collector (District Magistrate/Deputy Commissioner) of the district","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Chairperson of the Zilla Parishad","b":"Collector (District Magistrate/Deputy Commissioner) of the district","c":"Chief Executive Officer of the DDMA","d":"Superintendent of Police of the district"},"answer":"b"},{"a":"Chief executive member of the district council of the autonomous district","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Superintendent of Police","b":"Chief Medical Officer","c":"Chairperson of the Zilla Parishad","d":"Chief executive member of the district council of the autonomous district"},"answer":"d"},{"a":"Seven","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Six","b":"Nine","c":"Seven","d":"Eight"},"answer":"c"},{"a":"I and II only","e":"The chief executive officer of the DDMA is appointed by the state government, not the NDMA.","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"I and III only","b":"I, II and III","c":"I and II only","d":"II and III only"},"answer":"c"},{"a":"Advocates Act, 1961","e":"Being established by an Act of Parliament, the BCI is a statutory, not a constitutional, body.","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Advocates Act, 1961","b":"Legal Practitioners Act, 1961","c":"Legal Services Authorities Act, 1987","d":"Bar Council Act, 1953"},"answer":"a"},{"a":"Justice S.R. Das","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Justice H.R. Khanna","b":"Justice S.R. Das","c":"Justice J.L. Kapur","d":"M.C. Setalvad"},"answer":"b"},{"a":"Law Commission of India","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"National Commission to Review the Working of the Constitution","b":"First Administrative Reforms Commission","c":"Law Commission of India","d":"National Legal Services Authority"},"answer":"c"},{"a":"Union Ministry of Law and Justice","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Union Ministry of Home Affairs","b":"Union Ministry of Personnel","c":"Union Ministry of Law and Justice","d":"Union Ministry of Social Justice and Empowerment"},"answer":"c"},{"a":"Attorney-General of India and Solicitor-General of India","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Solicitor-General of India and Law Secretary","b":"Chief Justice of India and Attorney-General of India","c":"Law Secretary and Attorney-General of India","d":"Attorney-General of India and Solicitor-General of India"},"answer":"d"},{"a":"Two years","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Two years","b":"One year","c":"Three years","d":"Five years"},"answer":"a"},{"a":"Enrolment Committee","e":"The Enrolment Committee is a committee of the State Bar Councils, not the BCI; the BCI has a Legal Education Committee instead.","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Disciplinary Committee","b":"Enrolment Committee","c":"Legal Aid Committee","d":"Legal Education Committee"},"answer":"b"},{"a":"To recognise foreign law qualifications on a reciprocal basis for enrolment as an advocate","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"To entertain cases of misconduct against advocates on its roll","b":"To admit persons as advocates on its roll","c":"To promote the growth of Bar Associations","d":"To recognise foreign law qualifications on a reciprocal basis for enrolment as an advocate"},"answer":"d"},{"a":"two or more states, or for a state and a union territory","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"only two states at most","b":"group of states with more than 10,000 advocates","c":"two or more states, or for a state and a union territory","d":"only a state and its neighbouring union territory"},"answer":"c"},{"a":"24","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"28","b":"25","c":"24","d":"22"},"answer":"c"},{"a":"25","e":"A SBC with an electorate of five thousand has 15 members, one with five to ten thousand has 20 members, and one with more than ten thousand has 25 members; one-half of the elected members must have been advocates on a state roll for ten years.","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"15","b":"25","c":"30","d":"20"},"answer":"b"},{"a":"Five years","e":"If the SBC fails to hold elections before the term expires, the BCI may extend this term by a period of six months.","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Four years","b":"Five years","c":"Two years","d":"Three years"},"answer":"b"},{"a":"Additional Solicitor-General of India","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Attorney-General of India","b":"Advocate-General of Delhi","c":"Solicitor-General of India","d":"Additional Solicitor-General of India"},"answer":"d"},{"a":"Senior Advocates and other advocates","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Advocates-on-Record and other advocates","b":"Enrolled Advocates and Designated Advocates","c":"Senior Advocates and Advocates-on-Record","d":"Senior Advocates and other advocates"},"answer":"d"},{"a":"Chief Justice of India and the Judges","e":"A Permanent Committee constituted by the CJI deals with all matters relating to this designation, comprising the CJI as Chairperson, the two seniormost Supreme Court Judges, the Attorney-General for India, and a nominated member of the Bar.","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Bar Council of India","b":"Attorney-General of India","c":"Permanent Committee alone","d":"Chief Justice of India and the Judges"},"answer":"d"},{"a":"An Advocate-on-Record","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"An Advocate-on-Record","b":"Permission of the Attorney-General","c":"A written brief from the Bar Council","d":"A no-objection certificate from the SBC"},"answer":"a"},{"a":"1954","e":"When introduced in 1954, an Advocate of seven years standing was entitled to get registered as an Advocate-on-Record if he/she fulfilled the prescribed conditions; the Advocate-on-Record examination itself was introduced later, in 1959.","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"1959","b":"1954","c":"1961","d":"1950"},"answer":"b"},{"a":"1959","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"1961","b":"1959","c":"1963","d":"1954"},"answer":"b"},{"a":"instructed by an Advocate-on-Record or permitted by the Court","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"instructed by an Advocate-on-Record or permitted by the Court","b":"they hold a Senior Advocate designation","c":"they have practised for at least ten years","d":"they are members of the Bar Council of India"},"answer":"a"},{"a":"I, II and III","e":"There are 24 State Bar Councils in total, some covering multiple states/UTs jointly, such as the Bar Council of Arunachal Pradesh, Assam, Mizoram and Nagaland, and the Bar Council of Kerala (covering Kerala and Lakshadweep).","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"I and II only","b":"I, II and III","c":"II and III only","d":"I and III only"},"answer":"b"},{"a":"a non-statutory advisory body","e":"It is established by an order of the Central Government from time to time for a fixed tenure, and its recommendations are not binding on the government.","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"a constitutional body","b":"a quasi-judicial body","c":"a non-statutory advisory body","d":"a statutory body"},"answer":"c"},{"a":"Article 372","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Article 13","b":"Article 395","c":"Article 372","d":"Article 368"},"answer":"c"},{"a":"M.C. Setalvad","e":"M.C. Setalvad was the then Attorney-General of India; the term of this Commission was three years.","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Justice T.V. Venkatarama Aiyar","b":"Justice P.B. Gajendragadkar","c":"M.C. Setalvad","d":"Justice J.L. Kapur"},"answer":"c"},{"a":"Three years","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Five years","b":"Three years","c":"Two years","d":"Four years"},"answer":"b"},{"a":"First Law Commission (1834)","e":"See table below for the details of all four pre-independence Law Commissions.","table":{"headers":["Commission","Year Established","Chairman"],"rows":[["First","1834","Lord Macaulay"],["Second","1853","Sir John Romilly"],["Third","1861","Sir John Romilly"],["Fourth","1879","Dr Whitney Stokes"]]},"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Second Law Commission (1853)","b":"Fourth Law Commission (1879)","c":"Third Law Commission (1861)","d":"First Law Commission (1834)"},"answer":"d"},{"a":"Advocates Act","e":"The four pre-independence Commissions produced the Indian Penal Code, Criminal Procedure Code, Civil Procedure Code, Indian Contract Act, Indian Evidence Act, Transfer of Property Act, and other laws; the Advocates Act was enacted much later, in 1961.","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Transfer of Property Act","b":"Indian Evidence Act","c":"Advocates Act","d":"Indian Penal Code"},"answer":"c"},{"a":"Justice Ritu Raj Awasthi","e":"The 22nd Law Commission was constituted on 21st February, 2020, for a three-year term; its term was later extended up to 31st August, 2024.","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Justice A.P. Shah","b":"Justice Ritu Raj Awasthi","c":"Justice A.R. Lakshmanan","d":"Justice B.S. Chauhan"},"answer":"b"},{"a":"Indian Legal Service","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Indian Revenue Service","b":"Indian Legal Service","c":"Indian Police Service","d":"Indian Administrative Service"},"answer":"b"},{"a":"To identify laws which are no longer needed or relevant and can be repealed","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"To conduct elections to local bodies","b":"To appoint judges of the High Courts","c":"To draft the annual Union Budget","d":"To identify laws which are no longer needed or relevant and can be repealed"},"answer":"d"},{"a":"Ministry of Law and Justice","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Ministry of Parliamentary Affairs","b":"Ministry of Home Affairs","c":"Ministry of Law and Justice","d":"Ministry of Personnel"},"answer":"c"},{"a":"Boundary Commission","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Boundary Commission","b":"Constituency Commission","c":"Electoral Commission","d":"Territorial Commission"},"answer":"a"},{"a":"a statutory body","e":"It is established by the Central Government under a law enacted by Parliament, to demarcate boundaries of Parliamentary and Assembly Constituencies.","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"a statutory body","b":"a quasi-judicial tribunal","c":"an advisory body","d":"a constitutional body"},"answer":"a"},{"a":"President of India","e":"These orders have the force of law, cannot be challenged in any court, and modifications are not permissible even when laid before the Lok Sabha and the concerned State Legislative Assembly.","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Chief Election Commissioner","b":"President of India","c":"Prime Minister","d":"Union Home Minister"},"answer":"b"},{"a":"The Delimitation Commission Act, 1952","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"The Representation of the People Act, 1950","b":"The Delimitation Commission Act, 1962","c":"The Delimitation Act, 1972","d":"The Delimitation Commission Act, 1952"},"answer":"d"},{"a":"I, II and III","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"I and III only","b":"I, II and III","c":"II and III only","d":"I and II only"},"answer":"b"},{"a":"Articles 81, 82, 170, 330 and 332","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Articles 81, 82, 171, 330 and 331","b":"Articles 79, 80, 168, 325 and 326","c":"Articles 81, 82, 170, 330 and 332","d":"Articles 83, 85, 172, 331 and 333"},"answer":"c"},{"a":"84th Constitutional Amendment Act, 2001","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"73rd Constitutional Amendment Act, 1992","b":"91st Constitutional Amendment Act, 2003","c":"61st Constitutional Amendment Act, 1988","d":"84th Constitutional Amendment Act, 2001"},"answer":"d"},{"a":"2026","e":"This freeze also applies to the total number of existing seats in state Legislative Assemblies; however, seats reserved for SCs/STs were re-worked on the basis of the 2001 census.","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"2036","b":"2031","c":"2026","d":"2021"},"answer":"c"},{"a":"2001 census","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"1991 census","b":"2001 census","c":"1971 census","d":"2011 census"},"answer":"b"},{"a":"Justice Kuldip Singh","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Justice Ranjana Prakash Desai","b":"Justice Kuldip Singh","c":"Justice B.P. Jeevan Reddy","d":"Justice Kuldeep Kaur"},"answer":"b"},{"a":"2008","e":"The Commission had submitted its recommendations to the Government in 2007.","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"2009","b":"2008","c":"2002","d":"2007"},"answer":"b"},{"a":"Assam, Arunachal Pradesh, Manipur, Nagaland and Jharkhand","e":"The delimitation exercise was deferred in the four north-eastern states, while the Commission''s final order for Jharkhand was nullified.","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Assam, Bihar, Odisha, Kerala and Punjab","b":"Uttar Pradesh, Bihar, West Bengal, Assam and Tripura","c":"Sikkim, Tripura, Mizoram, Meghalaya and Goa","d":"Assam, Arunachal Pradesh, Manipur, Nagaland and Jharkhand"},"answer":"d"},{"a":"February 2020","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"February 2022","b":"February 2020","c":"March 2020","d":"March 2021"},"answer":"b"},{"a":"Justice Ranjana Prakash Desai","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Justice Ritu Raj Awasthi","b":"Justice Kuldip Singh","c":"Justice Ranjana Prakash Desai","d":"Justice B.S. Chauhan"},"answer":"c"},{"a":"The four north-eastern states","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Only Nagaland and Manipur","b":"The four north-eastern states","c":"Only Assam","d":"All eight north-eastern states"},"answer":"b"},{"a":"May 2022","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"February 2022","b":"March 2022","c":"May 2021","d":"May 2022"},"answer":"d"},{"a":"90","e":"Of these, 43 are in the Jammu region and 47 are in the Kashmir region; all 5 Parliamentary constituencies now have an equal number of 18 Assembly constituencies each.","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"111","b":"87","c":"90","d":"114"},"answer":"c"},{"a":"6","e":"One new Assembly constituency was created for the Kashmir region.","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"4","b":"7","c":"6","d":"5"},"answer":"c"},{"a":"Anantnag-Rajouri","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Anantnag-Rajouri","b":"Rajouri-Kashmir","c":"Poonch-Anantnag","d":"Jammu-Kashmir Central"},"answer":"a"},{"a":"9","e":"Of these, 6 are in the Jammu region and 3 are in the Kashmir region; 7 Assembly constituencies are separately reserved for the Scheduled Castes.","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"7","b":"9","c":"6","d":"3"},"answer":"b"},{"a":"North Eastern Council Act, 1971","e":"This Act repealed the earlier North Eastern Council Act, 1970, and came into force in 1972.","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"North Eastern Council Act, 1970","b":"North Eastern Areas (Reorganisation) Act, 1971","c":"North Eastern Council Act, 1972","d":"North Eastern Council Act, 1971"},"answer":"d"},{"a":"Sikkim","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Mizoram","b":"Meghalaya","c":"Tripura","d":"Sikkim"},"answer":"d"},{"a":"Shillong, Meghalaya","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Guwahati, Assam","b":"Itanagar, Arunachal Pradesh","c":"Shillong, Meghalaya","d":"Imphal, Manipur"},"answer":"c"},{"a":"Ministry of Development of the North Eastern Region (DONER)","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Ministry of Rural Development","b":"Ministry of Development of the North Eastern Region (DONER)","c":"Ministry of Home Affairs","d":"Ministry of Tribal Affairs"},"answer":"b"},{"a":"the Regional Planning Body for the north eastern region","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"a constitutional body","b":"a statutory tribunal","c":"the Regional Planning Body for the north eastern region","d":"the apex disaster management authority for the region"},"answer":"c"},{"a":"Union Home Minister","e":"The Minister (in-charge) of the Ministry of DONER serves as the ex-officio Vice-Chairman of the Council.","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Cabinet Secretary","b":"Minister of DONER","c":"Prime Minister","d":"Union Home Minister"},"answer":"d"},{"a":"I, II and III","e":"This reflects the original statutory scheme; since July 2018, however, the Union Home Minister has been designated ex-officio Chairman.","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"I and III only","b":"II and III only","c":"I and II only","d":"I, II and III"},"answer":"d"},{"a":"North Eastern Council Revitalisation Committee","e":"This Committee, headed by P.P. Shrivastav, submitted its report to the Government in 2004.","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Regional Planning Reforms Committee","b":"North Eastern Council Revitalisation Committee","c":"DONER Empowerment Committee","d":"North Eastern Development Committee"},"answer":"b"},{"a":"P.P. Shrivastav","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"P.P. Shrivastav","b":"Justice B.S. Chauhan","c":"M.C. Setalvad","d":"Veerappa Moily"},"answer":"a"}]') ON CONFLICT(chapter_slug) DO UPDATE SET subject_id=excluded.subject_id, chapter_number=excluded.chapter_number, title=excluded.title, answers_json=excluded.answers_json;
INSERT INTO chapter_content (chapter_slug, subject_id, chapter_number, title, answers_json) VALUES ('indian-polity-en-chapter-28-political-process-and-elections', 'indian-polity-en', 28, 'Political Process & Elections', '[{"a":"USA and Britain","e":"A one-party system exists in former communist countries like the USSR, while a multi-party system exists in countries like France, Switzerland and Italy.","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"France and Italy","b":"USSR and East European countries","c":"Switzerland and France","d":"USA and Britain"},"answer":"d"},{"a":"I, II and III","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"I and III only","b":"II and III only","c":"I and II only","d":"I, II and III"},"answer":"d"},{"a":"Election Commission","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Law Commission","b":"Union Ministry of Law and Justice","c":"Election Commission","d":"Delimitation Commission"},"answer":"c"},{"a":"registered-unrecognised party","e":"Such a party can select a symbol only from a list of free symbols, unlike national and state parties which are allotted reserved symbols.","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"registered-unrecognised party","b":"independent party","c":"provisional party","d":"sectional party"},"answer":"a"},{"a":"The Election Symbols (Reservation and Allotment) Order, 1968","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"The Conduct of Elections Rules, 1961","b":"The Registration of Political Parties Order, 1992","c":"The Election Symbols (Reservation and Allotment) Order, 1968","d":"The Representation of the People Act, 1951"},"answer":"c"},{"a":"I, II and III","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"I and III only","b":"II and III only","c":"I, II and III","d":"I and II only"},"answer":"c"},{"a":"25 seats","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"15 seats","b":"30 seats","c":"20 seats","d":"25 seats"},"answer":"d"},{"a":"Eight per cent","e":"This is a standalone vote-share condition, distinct from the six per cent vote-share conditions which require winning a minimum number of seats as well.","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Three per cent","b":"Six per cent","c":"Eight per cent","d":"Ten per cent"},"answer":"c"},{"a":"14","e":"On the eve of the Seventeenth Lok Sabha general elections (2019), there were 7 national parties and 52 state parties in the country.","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"10","b":"20","c":"7","d":"14"},"answer":"d"},{"a":"Indian National Congress","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Indian National Congress","b":"Shiromani Akali Dal","c":"Jammu & Kashmir National Conference","d":"Communist Party of India"},"answer":"a"},{"a":"Kanshi Ram","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Sharad Pawar","b":"Kanshi Ram","c":"Ram Vilas Paswan","d":"Mulayam Singh Yadav"},"answer":"b"},{"a":"I, II and III","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"II and III only","b":"I, II and III","c":"I and III only","d":"I and II only"},"answer":"b"},{"a":"A.B. Vajpayee and L.K. Advani","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"A.B. Vajpayee alone","b":"A.B. Vajpayee and M.G. Ramachandran","c":"A.B. Vajpayee and L.K. Advani","d":"L.K. Advani and Bal Thackeray"},"answer":"c"},{"a":"Telangana Rashtra Samithi (TRS)","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Janata Dal (Secular)","b":"YSR Congress Party","c":"Telugu Desam Party (TDP)","d":"Telangana Rashtra Samithi (TRS)"},"answer":"d"},{"a":"Tariq Anwar","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Tariq Anwar","b":"Mufti Mohd. Sayeed","c":"Sharad Yadav","d":"H.D. Deve Gowda"},"answer":"a"},{"a":"I, II and III","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"I and II only","b":"I and III only","c":"I, II and III","d":"II and III only"},"answer":"c"},{"a":"personalised parties","e":"The other categories of regional parties are those based on regional culture/ethnicity (e.g. Shiromani Akali Dal, DMK), those with an all-India outlook but lacking a national electoral base (e.g. Samajwadi Party), and those formed by a split in national parties (e.g. Biju Janata Dal, Trinamool Congress).","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"personalised parties","b":"all-India outlook parties","c":"ethnic parties","d":"split parties"},"answer":"a"},{"a":"Biju Janata Dal","e":"Other examples of this category include Rashtriya Janata Dal, Trinamool Congress and YSR Congress.","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Shiromani Akali Dal","b":"Asom Gana Parishad","c":"Telugu Desam","d":"Biju Janata Dal"},"answer":"d"},{"a":"I, II and III","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"I and III only","b":"I, II and III","c":"I and II only","d":"II and III only"},"answer":"b"},{"a":"They have widened the choice for voters in both parliamentary and assembly elections","e":"The latter three points are listed among the dysfunctions (negative aspects) of regional parties, not their positive role.","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"They are responsible for unresolved inter-state water disputes","b":"They have widened the choice for voters in both parliamentary and assembly elections","c":"They have encouraged casteism and linguism","d":"They have focused more on populist schemes affecting state economy"},"answer":"b"},{"a":"I and II only","e":"Regional parties have generally given more importance to regional interests rather than national interests, making statement (III) incorrect.","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"II and III only","b":"I, II and III","c":"I and II only","d":"I and III only"},"answer":"c"},{"a":"Part XV","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Part XIII","b":"Part XVI","c":"Part XIV","d":"Part XV"},"answer":"d"},{"a":"Article 324","e":"The power of superintendence, direction and conduct of elections to Parliament, state legislatures, and the offices of President and Vice-President is vested in the Commission.","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Article 325","b":"Article 327","c":"Article 324","d":"Article 326"},"answer":"c"},{"a":"18 years","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"16 years","b":"21 years","c":"18 years","d":"25 years"},"answer":"c"},{"a":"I, II and III","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"I and II only","b":"II and III only","c":"I and III only","d":"I, II and III"},"answer":"d"},{"a":"Article 323B","e":"In L. Chandra Kumar vs. Union of India (1997), the Supreme Court declared this provision (specifically the exclusion of jurisdiction clause) as unconstitutional; no such tribunal has been established so far.","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Article 329","b":"Article 323B","c":"Article 329A","d":"Article 324"},"answer":"b"},{"a":"Two","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Two","b":"Four","c":"Three","d":"One"},"answer":"a"},{"a":"President of India","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"President of India","b":"Prime Minister","c":"Parliament through a resolution","d":"Chief Justice of India"},"answer":"a"},{"a":"Chief Electoral Officer","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"District Election Officer","b":"Electoral Registration Officer","c":"Chief Electoral Officer","d":"Returning Officer"},"answer":"c"},{"a":"Returning Officer","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Chief Electoral Officer","b":"District Election Officer","c":"Returning Officer","d":"Presiding Officer"},"answer":"c"},{"a":"District Election Officer","e":"In the case of Union Territories, such appointments are made by the Returning Officers instead.","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Chief Electoral Officer","b":"Returning Officer","c":"Election Commission of India directly","d":"District Election Officer"},"answer":"d"},{"a":"Expenditure Observers","e":"General Observers keep a close watch on every stage of the electoral process, while Police Observers (IPS officers) monitor force deployment and law and order.","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"General Observers","b":"Expenditure Observers","c":"Police Observers","d":"Electoral Registration Observers"},"answer":"b"},{"a":"Six months","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Six months","b":"One year","c":"Three months","d":"Nine months"},"answer":"a"},{"a":"48 hours","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"24 hours","b":"48 hours","c":"36 hours","d":"72 hours"},"answer":"b"},{"a":"1998","e":"In 2003, all state elections and by-elections were held using EVMs, and the Commission took a historic decision to use only EVMs for the Lok Sabha election in 2004, using more than 1 million EVMs.","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"2004","b":"1989","c":"2003","d":"1998"},"answer":"d"},{"a":"Two kilometres","e":"No polling station is to deal with more than 1200 voters, and each polling station remains open for at least eight hours on the day of the election.","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Three kilometres","b":"One kilometre","c":"Two kilometres","d":"Five kilometres"},"answer":"c"},{"a":"Between two days before the start of polling and after the close of poll in any constituency","e":"Results of exit polls can only be published after half an hour of the end of polling hours on the last day of poll.","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Only on the day of polling","b":"Anytime during the election campaign","c":"Between two days before the start of polling and after the close of poll in any constituency","d":"One week before the start of polling"},"answer":"c"},{"a":"First-past-the-post system","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Mixed member proportional system","b":"Proportional representation system","c":"Single transferable vote system","d":"First-past-the-post system"},"answer":"d"},{"a":"High Court of the state involved","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"District Court","b":"High Court of the state involved","c":"Election Tribunal","d":"Supreme Court"},"answer":"b"},{"a":"Eighteen","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Sixteen","b":"Seventeen","c":"Fifteen","d":"Eighteen"},"answer":"d"},{"a":"BJP","e":"The BJP won 303 seats, well ahead of the Congress with 52 seats, in the 2019 general elections.","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"DMK","b":"BJP","c":"Trinamool Congress","d":"Congress"},"answer":"b"},{"a":"Article 329","e":"See table below for how Articles 324 to 329A relate to different aspects of the electoral system.","table":{"headers":["Article","Subject"],"rows":[["324","Superintendence, direction and control of elections vested in the Election Commission"],["325","No person ineligible for inclusion in electoral roll on grounds of religion, race, caste or sex"],["326","Elections to Lok Sabha and state assemblies on the basis of adult suffrage"],["327","Parliament''s power to make provision for elections to Legislatures"],["328","State Legislature''s power to make provision for elections to itself"],["329","Bar to interference by courts in electoral matters"],["329A","Special provision for elections of PM and Speaker (Repealed)"]]},"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Article 328","b":"Article 324","c":"Article 325","d":"Article 329"},"answer":"d"},{"a":"Allocation of seats in the House of the People and Legislative Assemblies/Councils of states","e":"This Act also conferred on the President the power to delimit constituencies after consultation with the Election Commission, and provided for the registration of electors.","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Conduct of elections and corrupt practices","b":"Registration of political parties","c":"Allocation of seats in the House of the People and Legislative Assemblies/Councils of states","d":"Disqualifications for defection"},"answer":"c"},{"a":"Representation of the People Act, 1951","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Election Laws (Amendment) Act, 2021","b":"Representation of the People Act, 1951","c":"Representation of the People Act, 1950","d":"Delimitation Act, 2002"},"answer":"b"},{"a":"2001 census","e":"The previous delimitation of Parliamentary and Assembly constituencies had been based on the 1971 census.","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"1971 census","b":"1991 census","c":"2011 census","d":"2001 census"},"answer":"d"},{"a":"Parliament (Prevention of Disqualification) Act, 1959","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Scheduled Castes and Scheduled Tribes Orders (Amendment) Act, 1976","b":"Representation of the People Act, 1951","c":"Government of Union Territories Act, 1963","d":"Parliament (Prevention of Disqualification) Act, 1959"},"answer":"d"},{"a":"Presidential and Vice-Presidential Elections Act, 1952","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Representation of the People Act, 1950","b":"Delimitation Act, 2002","c":"Government of National Capital Territory of Delhi Act, 1991","d":"Presidential and Vice-Presidential Elections Act, 1952"},"answer":"d"},{"a":"Registration of Electors Rules, 1960","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Registration of Electors Rules, 1960","b":"Members of Lok Sabha (Declaration of Assets and Liabilities) Rules, 2004","c":"Prohibition of Simultaneous Membership Rules, 1950","d":"Conduct of Elections Rules, 1961"},"answer":"a"},{"a":"1992","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"1992","b":"1985","c":"2004","d":"1968"},"answer":"a"},{"a":"61st Constitutional Amendment Act, 1988","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"84th Constitutional Amendment Act, 2001","b":"61st Constitutional Amendment Act, 1988","c":"73rd Constitutional Amendment Act, 1992","d":"44th Constitutional Amendment Act, 1978"},"answer":"b"},{"a":"1989","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"1989","b":"1998","c":"1993","d":"1996"},"answer":"a"},{"a":"1993","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"1993","b":"1989","c":"1998","d":"1996"},"answer":"a"},{"a":"National Front Government headed by V.P. Singh","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Janata Government headed by Morarji Desai","b":"United Front Government headed by Deve Gowda","c":"NDA Government headed by A.B. Vajpayee","d":"National Front Government headed by V.P. Singh"},"answer":"d"},{"a":"Six years","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Five years","b":"Ten years","c":"Three years","d":"Six years"},"answer":"d"},{"a":"Seven days","e":"Earlier, the death of any contesting candidate before polling led to the election being countermanded and restarted; this rule now applies only if the deceased did not belong to a recognised political party or the party doesn''t propose a replacement.","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Ten days","b":"Seven days","c":"Three days","d":"Fourteen days"},"answer":"b"},{"a":"Six months","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Three months","b":"One year","c":"Nine months","d":"Six months"},"answer":"d"},{"a":"14 days","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"21 days","b":"7 days","c":"14 days","d":"10 days"},"answer":"c"},{"a":"50","e":"For the Vice-Presidential election, the number was increased from 5 to 20, and the security deposit for both offices was raised from ₹2,500 to ₹15,000.","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"20","b":"100","c":"50","d":"30"},"answer":"c"},{"a":"I and II only","e":"Statement (III) relates to Presidential/Vice-Presidential elections (1997 reform), not Rajya Sabha elections.","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"I and II only","b":"II and III only","c":"I, II and III","d":"I and III only"},"answer":"a"},{"a":"₹2,000","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"₹10,000","b":"₹2,000","c":"₹1,000","d":"₹5,000"},"answer":"b"},{"a":"One per cent","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"Five per cent","b":"Two per cent","c":"One per cent","d":"Three per cent"},"answer":"c"},{"a":"2018","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"2017","b":"2016","c":"2018","d":"2019"},"answer":"c"},{"a":"I, II and III","e":"","table":null,"type":"mcq","options":{"a":"I, II and III","b"